/-!
# The formal spectrum of a relative completion along a finite type ring map

Let `S` be a scheme, let `A` be a weakly admissible topological ring over `S` and let
`A → A'` be a finite type ring map. **Stacks 0ANM** asserts three things about the relative
completion `(A')^ = lim_{I ⊆ A w.i.d.} A' / IA'`:

1. `(A')^` is a weakly admissible topological ring;
2. the induced morphism `Spf ((A')^) ⟶ Spf A` is representable;
3. that morphism is of finite type, because a morphism `T ⟶ Spf A` from a quasi-compact
   scheme factors through `Spec (A / I)` for some weak ideal of definition `I` (Stacks 0AIA)
   and then `T ×_{Spf A} Spf ((A')^) = T ×_{Spec (A / I)} Spec (A' / IA')`.

## Main results

* `TopologicalRing.finiteTypeModuloEveryWeakIdeal_canonicalMap`: the canonical map
  `A ⟶ (A')^` is taut, and `A / I → (A')^ / I(A')^ = A' / IA'` is a finite type ring map for
  every weak ideal of definition `I` of `A`. This is the ring-theoretic content of the third
  assertion; it is condition (a) of Stacks 0ANU for the canonical map.
* `FormalSpace.exists_isPullback_isFiniteTypeULift_formalSpectrumMap_of_factorsThroughStage`:
  the stage half of the implication (2) ⟹ (1) of **Stacks 0ANT** at an arbitrary point
  factoring through the stage rather than at the stage itself — the base change of `Spf (φ)`
  along such a point is represented by an object of the site and its projection is of finite
  type.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.exists_factorsThroughStage_of_compactSpace`: **Stacks 0AIA**
  for the canonical presentation of a formal spectrum — a point `T ⟶ Spf A` out of a
  quasi-compact object of the site factors through a stage `Spec (A / I) ⟶ Spf A`.
* `FormalSpace.exists_isPullback_isFiniteType_formalSpectrumMap_completionOver_of_compactSpace`:
  the source's base change identification, at a point `T ⟶ Spf A` out of a quasi-compact
  scheme of the site: `T ×_{Spf A} Spf ((A')^)` is represented by the object
  `T ×_{Spec (A / I)} Spec (A' / IA')` of the site, and its projection to `T` is of finite
  type.
* `FormalSpace.isRepresentableByAlgebraicSpacesULift_formalSpectrumMap_completionOver`:
  the second assertion in full — `Spf ((A')^) ⟶ Spf A` is representable by algebraic spaces.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isFiniteType_formalSpectrumMap_completionOver`: the third
  assertion in full — `Spf ((A')^) ⟶ Spf A` is of finite type.

The first assertion is `TopologicalRing.completionOver_isWeaklyAdmissible`, which this file
records as a clause of Stacks 0ANM; it is stated there with no finite type hypothesis, since
the relative completion of any ring map over a weakly admissible ring is weakly admissible.
The ring-theoretic form of the third assertion, that `(A')^` is topologically of finite type
over `A`, is `TopologicalRing.isTopologicallyOfFiniteType_canonicalMap`, likewise recorded
here as a clause of the tag.

## Implementation notes

The finite type statement for the quotients is the identification of `(A')^ / I(A')^` with
`A' / IA'`. The kernel of the projection `(A')^ → A' / IA'` is the closure of the ideal
generated by the image of `I`, which is the ideal appearing in
`TopologicalRing.FiniteTypeModuloEveryWeakIdeal`, and the projection is surjective, so that
quotient is `A' / IA'` through `RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective`. Finite type of
`A / I → A' / IA'` is then finite type of `A → A' → A' / IA'` with the source restricted
along the surjection `A → A / I`.

The factorization through a stage is Stacks 0AIA for the diagram of quotient spectra of the
quotient system, whose transition morphisms are thickenings. The form of Stacks 0AIA used is
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.exists_factor_through_closedImmersion_stage`, which asks only
that the transition morphisms be closed immersions and so does not need the set-theoretic
condition of Stacks 0AIS; the factorization it returns is a morphism of sheaves, and the
subcanonicity of the site turns it back into a morphism of the site.

### How the unqualified conclusions are reached

The source's representability and finite type conclusions are unqualified — the quasi-compact
`T` is a step in its argument, not a restriction on what it concludes — and they are proved
here unqualified. The step the source leaves tacit is that both conditions are local on the
target: its proof of Stacks 0AN5 (3) ⟹ (2) establishes the base change over each thickening
stage and then reads "since every morphism `T → Spf(A)` with `T` quasi-compact factors
through `Spec(A/I)` for some weak ideal of definition `I` (Lemma 0AIA) we conclude that
`Spf(φ)` is representable". That locality is
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.RepresentableFromAffinePoints`: an arbitrary
scheme-valued point is covered, surjectively and étale, by the coproduct of its affine opens,
over which the base change is the coproduct of the base changes over those affine opens.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0ANM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0ANM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AIA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AIA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AN5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AN5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AN6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AN6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0ANT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0ANT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0ANU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0ANU)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace TopologicalRing

universe u v

section Quotients

variable {B : Type u} {A : Type v} [CommRing B] [TopologicalSpace B] [CommRing A]

/-- The quotient of the relative completion by the kernel of the projection at a weak ideal of
definition `J` of the base is of finite type over `B ⧸ J` when `A` is of finite type over `B`.
The ideal is taken as a parameter together with an equation identifying it with that kernel,
so that the statement applies to the closure of the extended ideal without rewriting under a
proof of containment. -/
private theorem finiteType_quotientMap_canonicalMap
    (f : B →+* A) (hf : f.FiniteType) (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex B)
    (K : Ideal (CompletionOver f)) (hK : K = RingHom.ker (CompletionOver.projection f J))
    (h : J.1 ≤ Ideal.comap (CompletionOver.canonicalMap f) K) :
    (Ideal.quotientMap K (CompletionOver.canonicalMap f) h).FiniteType := by
  subst hK
  have hext : J.1 ≤ Ideal.comap f (extendedIdeal f J) :=
    Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mp le_rfl
  have hq : (Ideal.quotientMap (extendedIdeal f J) f hext).FiniteType := by
    refine RingHom.FiniteType.of_comp_finiteType (f := Ideal.Quotient.mk J.1) ?_
    rw [Ideal.quotientMap_comp_mk hext]
    exact hf.comp_surjective Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  set e := RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective (CompletionOver.projection_surjective f J)
  have hfwd : e.toRingHom.comp
      (Ideal.quotientMap (RingHom.ker (CompletionOver.projection f J))
        (CompletionOver.canonicalMap f) h) =
      Ideal.quotientMap (extendedIdeal f J) f hext := by
    refine RingHom.ext fun x ↦ ?_
    obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
    rfl
  have hfac : Ideal.quotientMap (RingHom.ker (CompletionOver.projection f J))
      (CompletionOver.canonicalMap f) h =
      e.symm.toRingHom.comp (Ideal.quotientMap (extendedIdeal f J) f hext) := by
    rw [← hfwd]
    exact RingHom.ext fun x ↦ (e.symm_apply_apply _).symm
  rw [hfac]
  exact (RingHom.FiniteType.of_surjective _ e.symm.surjective).comp hq

/-- **Stacks 0ANM.** Let `B` be a weakly pre-admissible linearly topologized ring and let
`f : B →+* A` be a finite type ring map. The canonical map from `B` to the relative completion
`A^ = lim_J A ⧸ JA` is taut, and for every weak ideal of definition `J` of `B` the induced
map `B ⧸ J → A^ ⧸ J A^` is of finite type; indeed `A^ ⧸ J A^ = A ⧸ JA`. This is condition (a)
of Stacks 0ANU for the canonical map. -/
@[stacks 0ANM "the relative completion along a finite type ring map is taut and of finite \
type modulo every weak ideal of definition of the base, which is the ring-theoretic content \
of the identification `T ×_{Spf A} Spf ((A')^) = T ×_{Spec (A / I)} Spec (A' / IA')`"]
theorem finiteTypeModuloEveryWeakIdeal_canonicalMap [IsTopologicalRing B]
    [IsLinearTopology B B] (f : B →+* A) (hB : IsWeaklyPreAdmissible B) (hf : f.FiniteType) :
    FiniteTypeModuloEveryWeakIdeal (CompletionOver.canonicalMap f) :=
  ⟨isTaut_canonicalMap f hB, fun J hJ ↦
    finiteType_quotientMap_canonicalMap f hf ⟨J, hJ⟩ _
      (CompletionOver.ker_projection_eq_closure f ⟨J, hJ⟩).symm _⟩

end Quotients

add_to_stacks 0ANM "the relative completion of a ring map over a weakly admissible \
topological ring is weakly admissible; no finite type hypothesis is needed"
  completionOver_isWeaklyAdmissible

add_to_stacks 0ANM "the relative completion along a finite type ring map is topologically of \
finite type over the base, which is the ring-theoretic form of the finite type assertion"
  isTopologicallyOfFiniteType_canonicalMap

end TopologicalRing

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace

universe u

variable {𝔅 : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : 𝔅.Contains S}
  {B A : Type u} [CommRing B] [TopologicalSpace B] [IsTopologicalRing B]
  [IsLinearTopology B B] [CommRing A]

section StageBaseChange

variable {C : Type u} [CommRing C] [TopologicalSpace C] [IsTopologicalRing C]
  [IsLinearTopology C C]

/-- **Stacks 0ANT**, the stage half of (2) ⟹ (1) at an arbitrary point factoring through the
stage, rather than at the stage itself. Let `φ : B ⟶ C` be a continuous homomorphism of weakly
admissible topological rings over `S` which is taut and of finite type modulo every weak ideal
of definition. For a point `U ⟶ Spec (B ⧸ I) ⟶ Spf B` of the formal spectrum, the base change
of `Spf (φ)` along it is represented by the object `U ×_{Spec (B ⧸ I)} Spec (C ⧸ K)` of the
site and the projection to `U` is locally of finite type and quasi-compact.

The base change is taken in the site, where `BigFppfOver.toScheme` preserves it, which is what
keeps the projection's finite type available: it is a base change of
`Spec (C ⧸ K) ⟶ Spec (B ⧸ I)`, and both halves of being of finite type are stable under base
change of schemes. The sheafified Yoneda embedding preserves fibre products too, so pasting the
resulting square with the stage square of
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isPullback_formalSpectrumMap_stage_of_isTaut` gives the square
over `Spf (φ)`. -/
theorem exists_isPullback_isFiniteTypeULift_formalSpectrumMap_of_factorsThroughStage
    (hB : TopologicalRing.IsWeaklyAdmissible B) (hC : TopologicalRing.IsWeaklyAdmissible C)
    (D : QuotientSystem 𝔅 S hS B) (E : QuotientSystem 𝔅 S hS C) (φ : ContinuousHom D E)
    (h : TopologicalRing.FiniteTypeModuloEveryWeakIdeal φ.toRingHom)
    (I : { I : Ideal B // TopologicalRing.IsWeakIdealOfDefinition I })
    (U : BigFppfOver 𝔅 S hS)
    (p : U ⟶ (BigAffineFppf.inclusion 𝔅 S hS).obj (D.stage I)) :
    ∃ (V : BigFppfOver 𝔅 S hS) (q : V ⟶ U)
      (r : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda (BigFppfOver.topology 𝔅 S hS)).obj V ⟶ formalSpectrum E),
      IsPullback r ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda (BigFppfOver.topology 𝔅 S hS)).map q)
        (formalSpectrumMap hB φ)
        ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda (BigFppfOver.topology 𝔅 S hS)).map p ≫
          formalSpectrumInclusion D I) ∧
      AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyOfFiniteType ((BigFppfOver.toScheme 𝔅 S hS).map q) ∧
      AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiCompact ((BigFppfOver.toScheme 𝔅 S hS).map q) := by
  classical
  let F := Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda (BigFppfOver.topology 𝔅 S hS)
  let _ : (BigFppfOver.topology 𝔅 S hS).Subcanonical := bigFppfOver_subcanonical 𝔅 S hS
  let _ : PreservesLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan F := by
    change PreservesLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan
      (uliftYoneda.{u + 1} (C := BigFppfOver 𝔅 S hS) ⋙
        presheafToSheaf (BigFppfOver.topology 𝔅 S hS) (Type (u + 1)))
    infer_instance
  let _ : PreservesLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan (BigFppfOver.toScheme 𝔅 S hS) :=
    Space.preservesLimitsOfShape_walkingCospan_toScheme 𝔅 S hS
  let _ : HasPullbacks (BigFppfOver 𝔅 S hS) := inferInstance
  obtain ⟨⟨Kv, hKw⟩, hKeq, hIK, hsq⟩ :=
    isPullback_formalSpectrumMap_stage_of_isTaut 𝔅 S hS hB hC D E φ h.1 I
  subst hKeq
  set w := (BigAffineFppf.inclusion 𝔅 S hS).map (φ.stageMap I ⟨_, hKw⟩ hIK) with hw
  have hinner : IsPullback (pullback.fst w p) (pullback.snd w p) w p :=
    IsPullback.of_hasPullback w p
  refine ⟨pullback w p, pullback.snd w p,
    F.map (pullback.fst w p) ≫ formalSpectrumInclusion E ⟨_, hKw⟩,
    ((hinner.map F).flip.paste_vert hsq.flip).flip, ?_⟩
  have hwlft : AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyOfFiniteType
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme 𝔅 S hS).map w) := by
    rw [hw]
    exact (show AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyOfFiniteType (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
      (Ideal.quotientMap (Ideal.map φ.toRingHom I.1).closure φ.toRingHom hIK))) from
      AlgebraicGeometry.HasRingHomProperty.Spec_iff.mpr (h.2 I.1 I.2))
  have hwqc : AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiCompact ((BigFppfOver.toScheme 𝔅 S hS).map w) := by
    rw [hw]
    exact (show AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiCompact (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
      (Ideal.quotientMap (Ideal.map φ.toRingHom I.1).closure φ.toRingHom hIK))) from
      inferInstance)
  exact ⟨MorphismProperty.of_isPullback (hinner.map (BigFppfOver.toScheme 𝔅 S hS)) hwlft,
    MorphismProperty.of_isPullback (hinner.map (BigFppfOver.toScheme 𝔅 S hS)) hwqc⟩

end StageBaseChange

omit [IsTopologicalRing B] [IsLinearTopology B B] in
/-- **Stacks 0AIA** for the canonical presentation of a formal spectrum: a point of `Spf B`
out of a quasi-compact object of the site factors through one of the quotient stages
`Spec (B ⧸ I) ⟶ Spf B`, by a morphism of the site. -/
theorem exists_factorsThroughStage_of_compactSpace
    (hB : TopologicalRing.IsWeaklyPreAdmissible B) (D : QuotientSystem 𝔅 S hS B)
    (U : BigFppfOver 𝔅 S hS) (hU : CompactSpace ((BigFppfOver.toScheme 𝔅 S hS).obj U))
    (a : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda (BigFppfOver.topology 𝔅 S hS)).obj U ⟶ formalSpectrum D) :
    ∃ (I : { I : Ideal B // TopologicalRing.IsWeakIdealOfDefinition I })
      (p : U ⟶ (BigAffineFppf.inclusion 𝔅 S hS).obj (D.stage I)),
      (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda (BigFppfOver.topology 𝔅 S hS)).map p ≫
        formalSpectrumInclusion D I = a := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨I₀, hI₀⟩ := hB
  let _ : Nonempty (OrderDual { I : Ideal B // TopologicalRing.IsWeakIdealOfDefinition I }) :=
    ⟨⟨I₀, hI₀⟩⟩
  let _ : IsDirected (OrderDual { I : Ideal B // TopologicalRing.IsWeakIdealOfDefinition I })
      (· ≤ ·) := weakIdeals_isDirected
  let _ : (BigFppfOver.topology 𝔅 S hS).Subcanonical := bigFppfOver_subcanonical 𝔅 S hS
  obtain ⟨M, t, ht⟩ := exists_factor_through_closedImmersion_stage 𝔅 S hS
    (OrderDual { I : Ideal B // TopologicalRing.IsWeakIdealOfDefinition I }) D.diagram
    (fun _ _ w ↦ (quotientSystem_transition_isThickening D (leOfHom w)).1)
    (colimit (formalSpectrumDiagram D)) (Iso.refl _) (yoneda.obj U)
    (isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda 𝔅 S hS U)
    (Space.isQuasiCompactSpace_yoneda_obj 𝔅 S hS hU) a
  obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ :=
    (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda_full (BigFppfOver.topology 𝔅 S hS)).map_surjective t
  refine ⟨OrderDual.ofDual M, p, ?_⟩
  refine ((congrArg (fun z ↦ z ≫ formalSpectrumInclusion D M) hp).trans ?_).trans ht
  exact congrArg (fun z ↦ t ≫ z) (Category.comp_id (formalSpectrumInclusion D M)).symm

/-- The base change of `Spf (g)` along a point out of a quasi-compact object of the site is
represented by an object of the site whose projection is locally of finite type and
quasi-compact. -/
private theorem exists_isPullback_lft_qc_formalSpectrumMap_completionOver
    (f : B →+* A) (hB : TopologicalRing.IsWeaklyAdmissible B) (hf : f.FiniteType)
    (D : QuotientSystem 𝔅 S hS B)
    (E : QuotientSystem 𝔅 S hS (TopologicalRing.CompletionOver f))
    (g : ContinuousHom D E) (hg : g.toRingHom = TopologicalRing.CompletionOver.canonicalMap f)
    (U : BigFppfOver 𝔅 S hS) (hU : CompactSpace ((BigFppfOver.toScheme 𝔅 S hS).obj U))
    (a : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda (BigFppfOver.topology 𝔅 S hS)).obj U ⟶ formalSpectrum D) :
    ∃ (V : BigFppfOver 𝔅 S hS) (q : V ⟶ U)
      (r : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda (BigFppfOver.topology 𝔅 S hS)).obj V ⟶ formalSpectrum E),
      IsPullback r ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda (BigFppfOver.topology 𝔅 S hS)).map q)
        (formalSpectrumMap hB g) a ∧
      AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyOfFiniteType ((BigFppfOver.toScheme 𝔅 S hS).map q) ∧
      AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiCompact ((BigFppfOver.toScheme 𝔅 S hS).map q) := by
  obtain ⟨I, p, hp⟩ := exists_factorsThroughStage_of_compactSpace hB.1 D U hU a
  obtain ⟨V, q, r, hsq, hlft, hqc⟩ :=
    exists_isPullback_isFiniteTypeULift_formalSpectrumMap_of_factorsThroughStage hB
      (TopologicalRing.completionOver_isWeaklyAdmissible f hB) D E g
      (hg ▸ TopologicalRing.finiteTypeModuloEveryWeakIdeal_canonicalMap f hB.1 hf) I U p
  exact ⟨V, q, r, hp ▸ hsq, hlft, hqc⟩

/-- **Stacks 0ANM**, the representability and the finite type assertions, at a point of
`Spf B` out of a quasi-compact scheme. Let `B` be a weakly admissible topological ring over
`S`, let `f : B →+* A` be a finite type ring map and let `g` present the canonical map
`B ⟶ A^` to the relative completion as a morphism of quotient systems over `S`. For every
point `T ⟶ Spf B` whose source is a quasi-compact object of the site, the base change
`T ×_{Spf B} Spf A^` is represented by an object `V` of the site — the source's
`T ×_{Spec (B / I)} Spec (A / IA)` — and the projection `V ⟶ T` is of finite type.

This is the source's own argument: the point factors through a stage `Spec (B / I) ⟶ Spf B`
by Stacks 0AIA, the base change along the factorisation is
`T ×_{Spec (B / I)} Spec (A / IA)`, and `Spec (A / IA) ⟶ Spec (B / I)` is of finite type
because `B / I → A / IA` is. -/
@[stacks 0ANM "the base change identification: for a point of `Spf A` out of a \
quasi-compact scheme `T` of the site, `T ×_{Spf A} Spf ((A')^)` is represented by the object \
`T ×_{Spec (A / I)} Spec (A' / IA')` of the site, and its projection to `T` is of finite type"]
theorem exists_isPullback_isFiniteType_formalSpectrumMap_completionOver_of_compactSpace
    (f : B →+* A) (hB : TopologicalRing.IsWeaklyAdmissible B) (hf : f.FiniteType)
    (D : QuotientSystem 𝔅 S hS B)
    (E : QuotientSystem 𝔅 S hS (TopologicalRing.CompletionOver f))
    (g : ContinuousHom D E) (hg : g.toRingHom = TopologicalRing.CompletionOver.canonicalMap f)
    (U : BigFppfOver 𝔅 S hS) (hU : CompactSpace ((BigFppfOver.toScheme 𝔅 S hS).obj U))
    (a : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda (BigFppfOver.topology 𝔅 S hS)).obj U ⟶ formalSpectrum D) :
    ∃ (V : BigFppfOver 𝔅 S hS) (q : V ⟶ U)
      (r : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda (BigFppfOver.topology 𝔅 S hS)).obj V ⟶ formalSpectrum E),
      IsPullback r ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda (BigFppfOver.topology 𝔅 S hS)).map q)
        (formalSpectrumMap hB g) a ∧
      Space.IsFiniteTypeULift.{u + 1} 𝔅 S hS ((uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).map q) := by
  obtain ⟨V, q, r, hsq, hlft, hqc⟩ :=
    exists_isPullback_lft_qc_formalSpectrumMap_completionOver f hB hf D E g hg U hU a
  exact ⟨V, q, r, hsq, Space.isFiniteTypeULift_uliftYoneda_map 𝔅 S hS q hlft hqc⟩

/-- The base change of `Spf (g) : Spf A^ ⟶ Spf B` along a point of `Spf B` out of a
quasi-compact object of the site is represented by an object of the site whose projection is
of finite type. This is the hypothesis the locality criteria of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.RepresentableFromAffinePoints` consume. -/
private theorem compactPullbackRepresentable_formalSpectrumMap_completionOver
    (f : B →+* A) (hB : TopologicalRing.IsWeaklyAdmissible B) (hf : f.FiniteType)
    (D : QuotientSystem 𝔅 S hS B)
    (E : QuotientSystem 𝔅 S hS (TopologicalRing.CompletionOver f))
    (g : ContinuousHom D E)
    (hg : g.toRingHom = TopologicalRing.CompletionOver.canonicalMap f) :
    CompactPullbackRepresentable 𝔅 S hS (formalSpectrumMap hB g) := by
  classical
  intro U hU ξ
  let _ : (BigFppfOver.topology 𝔅 S hS).Subcanonical := bigFppfOver_subcanonical 𝔅 S hS
  set η := Sheaf.uliftYonedaIsoSheafifiedYoneda (BigFppfOver.topology 𝔅 S hS) with hη
  obtain ⟨W, q, r, hsq, hlft, hqc⟩ :=
    exists_isPullback_lft_qc_formalSpectrumMap_completionOver f hB hf D E g hg U hU
      ((η.app U).inv ≫ ξ)
  have hnat : (η.app W).hom ≫
      (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda (BigFppfOver.topology 𝔅 S hS)).map q =
      (BigFppfOver.topology 𝔅 S hS).uliftYoneda.{u + 1}.map q ≫ (η.app U).hom :=
    (η.hom.naturality q).symm
  have hleft : IsPullback ((η.app W).hom)
      ((BigFppfOver.topology 𝔅 S hS).uliftYoneda.{u + 1}.map q)
      ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda (BigFppfOver.topology 𝔅 S hS)).map q) ((η.app U).hom) :=
    IsPullback.of_horiz_isIso ⟨hnat⟩
  refine ⟨W, q, (η.app W).hom ≫ r, ?_, hlft, hqc⟩
  have hpaste := hleft.paste_horiz hsq
  rwa [Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc] at hpaste

/-- **Stacks 0ANM**, the representability assertion. Let `B` be a weakly admissible
topological ring over `S`, let `f : B →+* A` be a finite type ring map and let `g` present
the canonical map `B ⟶ A^` to the relative completion as a morphism of quotient systems over
`S`. Then `Spf A^ ⟶ Spf B` is representable by algebraic spaces, which is condition (1) of
Stacks 0AN5 and the assertion Stacks 0AN6 makes about this morphism. -/
@[stacks 0ANM "representability of `Spf ((A')^) → Spf A`: the morphism is representable by \
algebraic spaces over `S`, with no restriction on the scheme-valued point of `Spf A` along \
which the base change is taken"]
theorem isRepresentableByAlgebraicSpacesULift_formalSpectrumMap_completionOver
    (f : B →+* A) (hB : TopologicalRing.IsWeaklyAdmissible B) (hf : f.FiniteType)
    (D : QuotientSystem 𝔅 S hS B)
    (E : QuotientSystem 𝔅 S hS (TopologicalRing.CompletionOver f))
    (g : ContinuousHom D E)
    (hg : g.toRingHom = TopologicalRing.CompletionOver.canonicalMap f) :
    Space.IsRepresentableByAlgebraicSpacesULift.{u + 1} 𝔅 S hS
      (formalSpectrumMap hB g).hom :=
  isRepresentableByAlgebraicSpacesULift_of_affine_pullback 𝔅 S hS (formalSpectrumMap hB g)
    (compactPullbackRepresentable_formalSpectrumMap_completionOver f hB hf D E g hg)

/-- **Stacks 0ANM**, the finite type assertion. With `B`, `f` and `g` as above,
`Spf A^ ⟶ Spf B` is of finite type: it is representable by algebraic spaces and every base
change of it along a scheme-valued point of `Spf B` is a morphism of algebraic spaces which
is of finite type.

The source's argument is the quasi-compact one — a point out of a quasi-compact scheme
factors through a thickening stage by Stacks 0AIA, and the base change along the
factorisation is `T ×_{Spec (B / I)} Spec (A / IA)`. The passage from there to an arbitrary
scheme-valued point is the locality of the two halves of being of finite type on the target,
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isLocallyOfFiniteTypeULift_pullback_of_compact_pullback` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isQuasiCompactULift_of_compact_pullback`. -/
@[stacks 0ANM "finite type of `Spf ((A')^) → Spf A`: the morphism is of finite type, with no \
restriction on the scheme-valued point of `Spf A` along which the base change is taken. The \
base change along a point out of a quasi-compact scheme `T` is the source's \
`T ×_{Spec (A / I)} Spec (A' / IA')`"]
theorem isFiniteType_formalSpectrumMap_completionOver
    (f : B →+* A) (hB : TopologicalRing.IsWeaklyAdmissible B) (hf : f.FiniteType)
    (D : QuotientSystem 𝔅 S hS B)
    (E : QuotientSystem 𝔅 S hS (TopologicalRing.CompletionOver f))
    (g : ContinuousHom D E)
    (hg : g.toRingHom = TopologicalRing.CompletionOver.canonicalMap f) :
    IsFiniteType 𝔅 S hS (formalSpectrumMap hB g) := by
  have hcpr := compactPullbackRepresentable_formalSpectrumMap_completionOver f hB hf D E g hg
  refine ⟨isRepresentableByAlgebraicSpacesULift_of_affine_pullback 𝔅 S hS
    (formalSpectrumMap hB g) hcpr, ?_⟩
  intro U ξ
  change Space.IsFiniteTypeULift.{u + 1} 𝔅 S hS
    (pullback.fst ξ (formalSpectrumMap hB g).hom)
  refine ⟨isLocallyOfFiniteTypeULift_pullback_of_compact_pullback 𝔅 S hS
    (formalSpectrumMap hB g) hcpr U ξ, ?_⟩
  intro Z hZ hZqc γ
  exact Space.isQuasiCompactSpaceULift_of_iso 𝔅 S hS
    (pullbackRightPullbackFstIso ξ (formalSpectrumMap hB g).hom γ).symm
    (isQuasiCompactULift_of_compact_pullback 𝔅 S hS (formalSpectrumMap hB g) hcpr Z hZ hZqc
      (γ ≫ ξ))

end AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace

end
